[00:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'That was awesome. I am here in Berlin, Germany for EPHA 2026 and I have a couple briefings to attend to check out some of the latest in tech, gadgets, and gaming. We\'re going to be hitting showstoppers to see some of the best tech here at the show and do some robot'

[00:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hunting because there are always some top tier robots [music] at Epha. Okay, let\'s go check it out. One of the most interesting gaming'

[00:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'handhelds I\'ve ever seen was just unveiled with Acer. And this is the Project Dual Play Mini. So, it is a concept, but the concept that they\'ve thought of is pretty cool. We have a handheld here. It\'s got the triggers, the fans, kind of the normal stuff that'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you\'d expect in a handheld, but [music] the plot twist here is you open it up from the middle and then you flip the screen forward and now you have a mini gaming laptop PC. Essentially, you can play the game fully with the keyboards. It\'s the same screen cuz you flipped it'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'forward. You have some speakers here on the side. And for what it\'s doing, it\'s a pretty good size given the fact that you have basically a mini laptop kind of ready to go. You can connect it to monitors. You can do your normal sort of PC tasks if you want. And then when you are ready to get back into handheld'

[01:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'gaming, you simply take the screen, flip it back, close it, and you are good to go. No info on specific specs or pricing or what\'s inside of this, but um I think Acer\'s cooking up something pretty'

[01:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'interesting. There is a product I had been hearing rumblings about from Nvidia that I was quite excited to check out. And I\'ll give you guys a quick spoiler. It\'s this over here, the Nvidia Spark. The really nice thing about the Nvidia Spark is'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that it\'s coming to multiple different brands and models of laptops. So, depending on what you\'re looking for in the product, you can still get the benefits of the chip within the form factor and the price range that makes the most sense for you. With how impressive the RTX Spark is when it'

[01:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'comes to those daily tasks and features, they\'re not compromising on gaming either, which of course Nvidia is very well known for. The RTX Spark still features things like DLSS5 support, ray reconstruction, frame generation that'

[01:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'gamers like myself are used to having on Nvidia GPUs, and it\'s nice to see them also supporting games that are running x86 chips through emulation. Given the fact that RTX Spark is an ARM chip, they\'re also thinking a lot about how we'

[02:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'like to use things on device. When it comes to AI, you\'re capable of running your own personal sort of AI chief of staff using RTX Spark. It can have personal context into things like your inbox, your contact calendar, or things'

[02:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that you may have been doing on a daily basis that it\'s made itself familiar with without having to go into the cloud. So, you get fast, quick responses while still getting excellent battery life. Okay, so we\'ve talked about things like AI models and gaming. What about'

[02:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'people like me who are just trying to find things for productivity? We saw demos with things like Photoshop where you\'re able to manipulate the image, turn it into something like nighttime, [music] and those layers in Photoshop become present for the user to'

[02:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'manipulate. So, it\'s going to save people a lot of time, and it was fast. It generated it very quickly with things like Blender, which was one of my favorite demos. As we move the image around on a nonRTX Spark device, we\'re seeing a lot of things needing to sort'

[03:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of render in real time and they become blurry with their RTX Spark. It supports DLSS 4.5 and ray reconstruction. So, we\'re seeing that as I move the model around, it stays very, very consistent. For those of you running Unreal Engine,'

[03:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can easily zoom out into a city and zoom back in and still get those ray tracing elements of detail. [music] And if you\'re looking to do something like take images and generate them into video, we saw with the RTX video nodes that they were able to cut the time down'

[03:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'from about 6 minutes for 1080p video at 60 fps to almost 2 minutes for a 2K video still at 60 fps. So productivity is definitely no slouch here on the RTX Spark. One of my favorite audio earbuds'

[03:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'ve ever tested is getting a follow-up. And I\'m actually wearing them right now, but you probably weren\'t even able to tell. These are the JAB JBuds Mini, but now with active noise cancellation.'

[03:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'They\'re still just as tiny as the originals were. They still have tons of fun colors, but this time, besides the active noise cancellation, which is obviously a very big deal, they\'re the first audio earbuds to support Apple Fine that aren\'t made by Apple'

[04:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'themselves. It\'s the JBuds Mini with active noise cancellation are actually available right now. But if you really like the gel design, these are going to be coming out in late October. But both are $42.99, so you can just choose what you like to your heart\'s content. Very'

[04:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'much my struggle at the moment as I cannot pick the color because they have so many amazing colors to choose from. Okay, I have done my product briefings and now I\'m here at Showstoppers, which always has a really great showcase of some of the coolest products at Epha.'

[04:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, let\'s go check it out and see what we can find. This is the Lumiar Carry. It\'s using its camera to intelligently detect different types of players that want to join in and give users the ability to choose the'

[04:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'types of mini gamess that they want to play, whether they\'re trying to have fun or improve as a basketball player. It\'s able to track your gestures, find the person who\'s able to then go ahead and receive the ball, take their shot, keep score, and have multiple friends join'

[04:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in. With the touchscreen, you have full functionality to customize what you want it to do, how many rounds you like to play, how long those rounds can play, etc. It is currently on Kickstarter for about $2,400, and they\'re targeting a release for this year. I\'m pretty bad at'

[05:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'basketball, but this is something that would make me enticed to see how bad I actually am. One of the signs that always catches my eye is Kodak. You know them for cameras, you know them for photography, but they\'re doing something pretty interesting. For the first time'

[05:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ever, they\'re jumping into the world of pets. So, this is the Kodak smart feeder. It is going to be able to watch your pet here on the camera and with the microphone, it can detect if, let\'s say,'

[05:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your dog barks, and you can quickly get a notification, check on your dog, perhaps even dispense some more food. On this side here, we have the water, and you can go ahead in the app, schedule when the food comes out, check on your animal. And in partnership with this'

[05:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'over here, you also have the ability to watch your pets with this camera. And it still gets the same alert functions. One camera stays steady in wide angle and the other will actually rotate and follow the animal around. This camera is'

[05:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'called the Kodak Duo Vision. It\'s going to be $79 and it\'s going to ship next month. Whereas this is the Kodak Smart Feeder. It\'s going to cost about $129 and start shipping in November. And both'

[06:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of them will be bundled together for about $179. We\'ve seen a lot of e- in devices, but Floica is cooking up something called the Verso, which basically stays on the back of your phone with Mags Safe and will give you things like reminders and'

[06:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'calendars based on the info that you\'re getting it. So, it is on device. You are going to be giving it the info. Press this button to record long conversations and this button right here will act sort of like a microphone to give it more data. These devices will come in a black'

[06:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and silver colorway around December and they\'re looking at about a $240 range in terms of pricing. Because it is fully on device and not connecting to your actual phone, I like the fact that you can take this with you to go ahead and record a'

[06:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'meeting or give it a quick note. And with its e- in display, you don\'t have to worry about it dying during the day. 72 hours is a pretty beefy battery life. So, this definitely has my attention. A lot of people have tried to make power banks for charging, but Bellein\'s doing'

[07:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'something very interesting here where they\'re thinking about the safety and long-term reliability of their power banks. This is the Ultracharge Pro Slim and the Ultra Charge Pro. The Ultra Charge Pro Slim has a very nice MagSafe design, very thin with nice rubber'

[07:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'textures, and holds 5,000 milliamps of charge. And the Ultraarge Pro holds 10,000 milliamps. Still has a nice design. No Mag Safe, but you get a very nice display which you can cycle through for different modes such as how much'

[07:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'charge is left, the battery life, and looking at thermal management. Now, what makes these so unique compared to other battery packs is that they have a semiolid state drive. Basically, there is a layer of gel inside which is going to help with durability and damage'

[07:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'protection. So, this will not explode if a nail goes through it is what I\'ve been told. And we\'re not going to be testing that today, but I very much am going to be taking their word for it. Because of that design as well, it means that after 1,000 cycles, you still have over 80% of the lifespan left. The Ultracharge Pro'

[07:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Slim retails for $70 and the Ultracharge Pro retails for 90 and they will be out in September. AI in a coffee machine might seem like overkill, but what they\'re doing over here at Nunk is'

[08:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pretty cool. Essentially, it\'s using AI to perfectly scan the beans that you\'re putting into the machine, tell how fresh it is, and use that data to factor into how it grinds it. There are beans that you can add in that are directly'

[08:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'compatible with the device. But let\'s say you\'ve bought a different brand. You simply go into the app, take a photo, and scan it, and implement that information into the app. It\'s able to say things like how dark the roast is, when you bought it, the size of it, and if anything\'s wrong, you simply just go'

[08:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ahead and add it in. It gets better all the time with software updates, which are free, by the way. It\'s currently at a €2,700 price point. It\'s been up for sale in Europe since September, but they are hoping to bring it to the United States later next year. As an obsessed'

[08:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'coffee drinker, I do quite like the idea of having something that will always taste good, even as the beans slowly come to an end because depending where you buy those beans, they\'re not cheap. Showstoppers is always full of pretty incredible concepts. And this is a'

[08:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'concept that I very much enjoy, a bezelless phone. So, finally, the entire screen real estate. We have basically no bezels. But they weren\'t done yet. They also decided to put a very interesting design here on the back. I don\'t think it\'ll get picked up as much on the'

[09:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'camera, but these butterflies genuinely look like they are popping out of the back. So, I am very much rooting for them. Techno is cooking here. Hopefully, this concept can one day become a real phone that I can go ahead and pull out of my pocket. Showstoppers was excellent'

[09:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'last night. It is now Friday and I am hitting the show floor to do something that I\'m very excited to do. Robot hunting. EA always has incredible robots. So, we\'re going to go inside. I think I saw a dancing robot. So, we\'re'

[09:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'going to go that way and check it out and see uh what\'s what. Let\'s go. The Anker Yui Robot Lawn Mower S2 Max is here at the show, coming later next year'

[09:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in the United States. This one is by far the most advanced model that they\'ve made. And what I love about these specific products is that they save me from actually having to do the chore myself. So, I like it when they get more complex. This one is going up a slope like it is no problem. Hopefully, one'

[10:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'day they\'ll make one that takes out the trash, too. Robots have figured out how to climb'

[10:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'stairs. [music]'

[10:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The Robbo Rock Saros Rover. No planned release date or price yet, but it is a robot vacuum that can go up the stairs and slide down. That was much smoother than I expected.'

[10:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I very much thought that thing was going to haul down that ramp, but it controlled itself really well. And it\'s back to just cleaning. Two things from robotics that I love to see at Epha. Things that are helpful and things that are world firsts. This is the world\'s first twoin one where we'

[10:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'have the circular motor that is providing the liquid to the window and then this square part here is going to move around and dry those areas. It\'s called the Hut 10S and they\'ve made other models in the past as well as'

[11:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'other worlds first. They\'re targeting a release date of November for this year and about $400. Oh yeah, we should probably stop recording before I watch this all day. Two of the most common things inside of a content creator\'s kit, a gimbal and a drone. But what if the gimbal could fly?'

[11:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Well, that\'s what\'s going on here with the Hover Air Versa. It\'s going to take off and track me and follow me as I walk. Okay, we have the red light. So, now it'

[11:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is going to follow me. Stays locked on.'

[11:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And it still knows it was me. That guy walked through, but it recognized that was still me. That was awesome. They\'re hoping to'

[12:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bring this to the United States at some point pending FCC approval, but right now it\'s available in Europe for about €400 with a release date of about October. And it also got one of our best in the show at Epha 2026 from Tom\'s Guide. And that wraps up EPHA 2026 here'

[12:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in Berlin, Germany. I got to see a lot of really cool things, some things that did not get to make it here in the video. But be sure to stay tuned here on Tom\'s Guide and our social platforms for all the amazing things that myself and'

